 5 files changed, 176 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)
commit 4364832b9be133015daee0638b21378808d9dd61
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Aug 11 11:49:29 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Aug 11 11:49:29 2026 -0500

    fix(loops): S4 review r2 — materialize at resolution in store verbs, change-fact never fails the mutation
    
    Two confirmed findings from the S4-flip review:
    
    1. store.py's local resolve_store_path still used the pure
       engine.residence.resolve_store_path, so fix #3 (materialize at
       resolution) never reached the store verbs. On a fresh clone of a
       JSONL-canonical vertex — log tracked, derived .db not — ticks/stats
       reported "not yet materialized — no facts emitted" for a store with
       facts, and verify tracebacked with an uncaught FileNotFoundError.
       Routing the .vertex branch through resolved_index converts every
       consumer at one seam: _require_materialized_store, make_fetcher,
       export, reindex, absorb/adopt CAS reads. With no log to build from
       the index stays absent, so the not-yet-materialized contract still
       speaks for a genuinely never-emitted store.
    
    2. JsonlCanonicalUnsupported raised from the JsonlStore constructor
       (catch-up runs in __init__) escaped _maybe_emit_change, so sl add /
       sl rm tracebacked AFTER the .vertex rewrite had landed — violating
       the function's own contract that diagnostics never fail the
       mutation. The emit block now degrades to a stderr warning carrying
       the exception text verbatim, which is what tells the user their
       derived index holds rows the log never saw.
    
    Regression tests verified failing pre-fix: 3 store-verb fresh-clone
    tests (FileNotFoundError at store.py:96), 2 add/rm poisoned-index tests.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

