Focused scratch experiments found four reproducible correctness gaps despite the regression suite: an existing derived index is not tailed during read resolution; an earlier indexed row can be edited without detection; a post-fsync metadata/commit failure can be stamped past by the next append on the same handle; and the codec accepts duplicate keys while its serializer can emit rows its decoder rejects. I’m running the package suites now, then I’ll distinguish regressions that genuinely pass from these uncovered cases.
